well%2C%20in%20my%20quick%20off-the%20cuff%20comment%2C%20i%20don%27t%20think%20i%20stated%20that%20i%0Athought%20%22peter%20jackson%20is%20a%20jerk%21%22%20although%20i%20understand%20that%20this%20has%0Abeen%20the%20reaction%20of%20some.%20but%20i%20do%20think%20that%20he%20didn%27t%20truly%20understand%0Athe%20books.%20watching%20the%20interviews%20with%20him%2C%20both%20sets%2C%20for%20each%20movie%2C%20he%0Aand%20the%20main%20actors%20in%20the%20film%20seem%20completely%20unaware%20of%20tolkein%27s%20very%0Acatholic%20worldview%2C%20and%20absolutely%20unaware%20of%20tolkein%27s%20deliberate%20inclusion%0Aof%20catholic%20themes%20and%20symbolism.%20they%20seem%20to%20be%20treating%20the%20ideas%20in%20the%0Abook%20as%20half%20action-adventure%20%2F%20half%20new-age-style%20mythology.%20john%20rhys%0Adavies%20interview%20was%20most%20indicative%20of%20this.%20so%2C%20yes%2C%20i%20do%20believe%20that%0Ajackson%20did%20not%20understand%20tolkein%2C%20and%20missed%20many%20of%20the%20core%20messages%20of%0Athe%20books.%20he%20does%20well%20on%20the%20surface%2C%20but%20hasn%27t%20even%20begun%20to%20plumb%20the%0Adepths.%20he%20loses%20a%20lot%2C%20and%20thus%2C%20so%20do%20we%20all.%20still%2C%20it%20is%20a%20very%20good%0Awork%20of%20film.%0Ai%20do%20take%20exception%2C%20a%20bit%2C%20to%20your%20description%20of%20faramir%20and%20his%20interlude%0Awith%20frodo%2C%20sam%2C%20and%20golum%20as%20a%20%22tea%20break%22%20as%20written%20it%20worked%20well%0Aeven%20for%20a%20clueless%20audiance%20who%20is%20geared%20more%20for%20visual%20special%20effects%2C%0Athan%20for%20finding%20deep%20meaning%20in%20a%20story...%20there%27s%20a%20battle%2C%20a%20capture%20with%0Athe%20hobbits%20scared%20out%20of%20their%20minds%2C%20golum%20is%20nearly%20killed%2C%20faramir%20finds%0Aout%20about%20the%20ring%2C%20and%20teeters%20on%20the%20cusp%20didn%27t%20need%20an%20extra%20nazgul%0Abattle.%20but%20yes%2C%20since%20it%20just%20ended%20right%20there%2C%20w%2Fo%20any%20of%20the%20